      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let \\( F \\) be the force in pounds and \\( L \\) be the length of the handle in inches. According to the inverse variation formula, \\( F \\times L = k \\), where \\( k \\) is a constant.\n\n1. **Find the constant \\( k \\):**\n   Given that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force, we can substitute these values into the formula:\n   \\[\n   F \\times L = k\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   375 \\times 9 = k\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   k = 3375\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the force needed for a 15-inch wrench:**\n   We need to find the force \\( F \\) required to loosen the bolt with a 15-inch handle. Using the formula \\( F \\times L = k \\) again, we substitute \\( L = 15 \\) and \\( k = 3375 \\):\n   \\[\n   F \\times 15 = 3375\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( F \\):\n   \\[\n   F = \\frac{3375}{15}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   F = 225\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the force required to loosen the bolt with a 15-inch handle is \\(\\boxed{225}\\) pounds.",
