    "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the concept of inverse variation. Inverse variation means that as one quantity increases, the other quantity decreases, and vice versa. In this case, the force needed to loosen the bolt (F) varies inversely with the length of the handle (L). This relationship can be expressed mathematically as:\n\nF * L = k\n\nwhere k is a constant.\n\nFirst, we need to find the value of k using the given information. We know that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force to loosen the bolt. So, we can plug these values into the equation:\n\n375 * 9 = k\n\nk = 3375\n\nNow that we have the value of k, we can use it to find the force needed to loosen the bolt with a handle length of 15 inches. We can plug this new value into the equation:\n\nF * 15 = 3375\n\nTo solve for F, we divide both sides of the equation by 15:\n\nF = 3375 / 15\n\nF = 225\n\nSo, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require 225 pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
